NNOOTTEESS
       The PPTTHHRREEAADD__SSCCOOPPEE__SSYYSSTTEEMM contention scope typically indicates that a
       user‐space thread is bound directly to a single kernel‐scheduling
       entity.  This is the case on Linux for the obsolete LinuxThreads
       implementation and the modern NPTL implementation, which are both 1:1
       threading implementations.

       POSIX.1 specifies that the default contention scope is implementation‐
       defined.

